From 9b935c66a775f39bc85b5294cd4fbd6879e1e2d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:16:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(2d): one contour-parallel ring set for Pass starts at
 Auto, Inside and Outside

An area round a part (the 2D Offset Outside band) now has one ring set
for every start side: the offsets of the part, clipped to the
cutter-centre area. Inside walks it from the part out, as before.
Outside walks the same pieces mirrored (each piece reversed so climb
stays climb, the outer edge first, the part wall last), so no ring
piece ends on the part wall any more. Auto picks one of the two sides
in one place (ring_side::resolve): Outside when the stock box leaves
the outer edge in air, else Inside. The resolved side drives the rings,
the links and the entry, so Auto is exactly the path of one side.

Pockets, the 3-D levels and the Adaptive plan keep their plans. The
entry (#3746), the links (#3747) and the dead-end ramp (#3748) do not
change. Decision: docs/decisions/3744-one-ring-set.md.

Fixes #3744

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
